<title>SINGAPORE: FCC wins land tender at S$275.56 mln.</title>
<headline>FCC wins land tender at S$275.56 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Capital Corp (FCC) said on Tuesday it had won a government tender for a 99-year lease on a 34,949.2 square metre block of land in Singapore at S$275.56 million.</p>
<p>FCC said in a statement it would form a company with Teamfine Enterprises Ltd to build a residential development on the site.</p>
<p>It said it would hold 90 percent of the equity in the new company and Teamfine, a wholly owned subsidiary of Hong Kong property giant Hysan Development Company Ltd, would hold the remaining 10 percent. ($1 = S$1.40)</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
